// DRAFT (Act III, planning only). Ch19 I09 "The engine stops" (C, 2 min) and I10 "The eye opens" (C, 1 min).
// act3_ch19.md §2 I09-I10. Liss shuts the anchor-engine down: a Lit Age lever and three held inputs. The spire's lamps
// DON'T go out (they're bound; only H09 frees them) but they STOP BEING FED: the hum stops. RULE 4: the Wardens lie
// still, their light held in them; NOTHING RISES. Toma closes Hesper Oan's eyes. Then from the crown, far out at sea,
// the storm wall turns and a calm opens at its centre: a well of dark water going down.
title: ch19_the_engine_stops
location: ch19/iskarra_spire
---
@letterbox on
@camera I07
@music engine_down fade=1.0
@mark liss engine_lever walk
@letterbox off
<<event hold_input lever_one>>
@anim liss pull engine_lever
@wait 2.5
<<event hold_input_end>>
<<event hold_input lever_two>>
@wait 2.5
<<event hold_input_end>>
<<event hold_input lever_three>>
@sfx engine_hum_stops
@wait 3.0
<<event hold_input_end>>
@letterbox on
@camera I08
@vfx glimmer_held at=wardens count=12
@wait 3.0
Liss [neutral]: That's the first one. #line:ch19_engine_001
@wait 2.0
@mark toma hesper_oan walk
@anim toma close_eyes hesper_oan
@wait 4.0
<<set $ch19_engine_stopped = true>>
@camera I09
@music the_eye fade=2.0
@wait 6.0
Kerrid [neutral]: There's the stair. #line:ch19_engine_002
@wait 3.0
<<set $ch19_complete = true>>
@fade out 2.0
@letterbox off
===
